      <span class="blog-post__tag blog-post__tag--blue">Finance</span>
      <h1 class="blog-post__title">My AI briefs me on gold, oil, and markets every morning.</h1>
      <p class="blog-post__subtitle">Every morning, my AI sends me a market briefing: gold, oil, S&amp;P 500, Hang Seng, Nikkei — with daily change percentages, context on what moved the markets, and what it means for my portfolio. No financial app needed.</p>
      <div class="blog-post__meta">
        <span>April 2026</span>
        <span>·</span>
        <span>2 min read</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="blog-post__hero-image">
      <img src="/images/blog-daily-market-brief.png" alt="AI daily market briefing showing gold oil and indices">
    </div>

    <div class="blog-post__content">
      <p>Working in transpacific trade, I need to stay on top of global markets — not just for trading, but because commodity prices directly affect shipping costs, supplier pricing, and contract negotiations.</p>

      <p>The old way: open Bloomberg, check gold, check oil, check US indices, check Asian indices. Scroll through headlines. Piece together the story yourself. Maybe 15-20 minutes every morning.</p>

      <p>Now I get one message. Here's what it looked like on April 9, 2026:</p>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <p><strong>Daily Market Brief — 9 April 2026, 12:31 PM HKT</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Gold (XAU/USD):</strong> ~$4,835/oz | Daily: +2.7% | MTD: +3.5% | QTD: -4.4% | YTD: ~+1%</p>
        <p>Gold hit an all-time high of $5,061 on Feb 11; currently retracing amid geopolitical de-escalation.</p>
        <br>
        <p><strong>Brent Oil:</strong> ~$93.90/bbl | Daily: -14% | MTD: -12% | QTD: +18% | YTD: +25%</p>
        <p>Crashed after US-Iran 2-week ceasefire deal and Strait of Hormuz reopening. Steepest oil drop in ~6 years.</p>
        <br>
        <p><strong>Key Indices:</strong></p>
        <p><strong>S&amp;P 500:</strong> 6,616.85 (+0.08%, futures +2.7%)</p>
        <p><strong>Dow Jones:</strong> 46,584.46 (-0.18%, futures +2.5%)</p>
        <p><strong>Nasdaq:</strong> 22,017.85 (+0.10%, futures +3.3%)</p>
        <p><strong>Hang Seng:</strong> ~22,900 (+2.95%)</p>
        <p><strong>Nikkei 225:</strong> 56,308.42 (+5.39%)</p>
      </div>

      <p>One message. Gold, oil, five indices. Plus the context — <em>why</em> oil crashed (US-Iran ceasefire), <em>where</em> gold is relative to its high, <em>what</em> futures are signaling for the next session.</p>

      <h2>Not just numbers — context</h2>

      <p>A raw price feed is useless without context. My AI doesn't just dump numbers — it adds the story behind the moves:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Geopolitical drivers</strong> — &ldquo;Oil crashed after US-Iran ceasefire deal&rdquo; — tells me this isn't a normal market move</li>
        <li><strong>Historical context</strong> — &ldquo;Steepest oil drop in ~6 years&rdquo; — tells me the magnitude</li>
        <li><strong>Futures vs cash</strong> — S&amp;P closed flat but futures are +2.7% — tells me what to expect at the next open</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-timeframe view</strong> — daily, MTD, QTD, YTD — tells me if this is a blip or a trend</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Fully customizable</h2>

      <p>The briefing is configured to my needs. I can:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Add or remove assets</strong> — add VIX, USD/JPY, copper, or any commodity I'm tracking</li>
        <li><strong>Change delivery time</strong> — 7 AM before I wake up, or 9 AM just before market open</li>
        <li><strong>Add alerts</strong> — &ldquo;flag if gold breaks $5,000 or oil drops below $90&rdquo;</li>
        <li><strong>Change format</strong> — brief summary or detailed breakdown</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who is this for?</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Procurement and trade professionals</strong> — commodity prices affect your costs directly</li>
        <li><strong>Investors with day jobs</strong> — stay informed without living in a finance app</li>
        <li><strong>Business owners</strong> — understand how macro moves affect your business planning</li>
      </ul>

      <p>You don't need a Bloomberg terminal. You need an AI that reads one and tells you what matters — in one message, every morning.</p>

      <h2>Highlights and suggested actions</h2>

      <p>Beyond raw data, the AI can also pull highlights from publications like The Economist and suggest actions based on your portfolio:</p>

      <div class="blog-post__inline-image">
        <img src="/images/blog-economist-highlight.png" alt="AI highlighting Economist article with suggested action" loading="lazy">
      </div>

      <p>The AI doesn't just summarize — it connects the dots between global news and your specific positions. You get the insight <em>and</em> the action item in one message.</p>
    </div>

